# 10. PLAYER INFLUENCE SYSTEM

The player is an observer, creator and indirect controller.

Do not force the player into direct character control as the primary gameplay mechanic.

Allow the player to influence reality through natural language.

Examples:

"Make everyone in the town believe that a mysterious creature lives in the forest."

"Give the mayor a secret ambition to become the most powerful person in the country."

"Make two rival characters accidentally discover that they share the same secret."

"Create a serious shortage of food."

"Give one character an opportunity to become extremely wealthy."

"Make the town experience a period of peace after years of conflict."

The AI must interpret the instruction and apply appropriate world changes.

### Important distinction

The player can establish circumstances, goals, tendencies and events.

However, characters should retain their autonomy.

For example, instructing a character to become friends with someone should influence their behaviour, not automatically guarantee a genuine friendship.

The simulation should determine whether the relationship develops naturally.

